We're moving off the net next week, and I've been a faithful reader
(and player) for over a year.  Maybe I'll get back on someday, but
I'll miss all the FAQ's.  Since I won't be around, I'll throw out a
few ideas I had during the last game:

POSSIBLE SPOILERS AHEAD:


(1) SLEEPING
Suppose the characters had to sleep in the dungeon?  Yes, I hear the
howls of protest -- sleeping is boring, dangerous, etc.  But sleeping
is already built in in some ways and _could_ be a lot of fun.  Right
now it's just a trap. Fer instance:

	(A) SPELL-CASTING
	We had a long killer discussion about spells and how dumb
	they are -- well, they are!  Anybody out there ever win a game
	by using spellbooks?  What if you got the spells back after
	you slept?  Then you could use spells more than once every hour
	of playing time, and wizards would be a force to be reckoned
	with.  A spellbook would be worthwhile, not just a means to
	teleport :-).
	(B) NEW ITEMS
	Coffee
	Amulet of Wakefulness

I admit I just like the idea.  After all, your pets could protect you
while you slept, or you could lock yourself in one of those mysterious
little rooms until you woke up.  It makes a skeleton key a really
useful item.

(2) ALIGNMENT
OK, here's a tough question: does anyone out there really play a
Lawful, Neutral or Chaotic character?  I know I don't.  How many
Lawfuls can't wait to find a shop to pillage?  Me, for sure.  I never
pass up the opportunity for shoplifting if I think there's a pair of
speed boots, gauntlets of power or (heaven forbid!) an artifact or a
WoW.  I don't really want to have this checked by the game, but
alignment is really just a way to segregate altars.

When I am in good standing with the Lawful god, and put on a helm of
alignment change, it looks like I am in good standing with my new god.
Does this make sense?



Well, that's it for now.  I'll try to find a way to get 3.1 when it
comes out.  Oh yeah, just today I tried to force a chest with a
bullwhip (dumb idea in the first place) and I destroyed the chest!!
A new one on me.  Thanks a lot for the game, dev team, and thanks
everyone else for the writing (what's up Dave, you've been quiet
recently!)

Allen


